Ner = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ner) (e:~’ tapa Abner leh Saul’ tapa) (r:10.2.12/9.14.51) (q:draft)
Oliv = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:olive) (d:oliv written with a capital, mostly in Oliv Mual, the Mount of Olives) (e:Zeisu ~ Mual ah a pai hi) (b:oliv) (r:43.8.1/42.19.29) (q:draft)
Ompihna = (t:n) (w:presence) (d:being with someone; in the Bible in Ompihna Anlum, the bread of the Presence set before God) (e:~ Anlum adingin sabuai kham) (r:13.28.16/2.25.30) (q:draft)
Hur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hur) (e:~ in Uri’ pa hi a) (r:13.2.20/2.31.2) (q:draft)
Mun = (t:n) (w:Place/place) (d:mun written with a capital in titles of places such as Siangthopen Mun, the Most Holy Place) (e:Siangtho Bel ~ kici dei khat) (b:mun) (r:58.9.3/26.41.23) (q:draft)
Pen = (t:part) (w:most) (d:superlative marker placed after a describing word, written with a capital in titles of God such as Sang Pen Pasian, God Most High) (e:amah in Sang ~ Pasian’ siampi zong) (b:pen) (r:1.14.18/44.7.48) (q:draft)
Sang = (t:adj) (w:high) (d:sang written with a capital in titles of God: Sang Penpa and Sang Pen Pasian, the Most High) (e:~ Penpa tungah na thuciamnate uh bawl) (b:sang) (r:19.50.14/19.82.6) (q:draft)
Bani = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Bani) (e:a pa Amzi, a pa ~, a pa Shemer) (r:13.6.46/15.2.10) (q:draft)
Gungal = (t:n) (w:Trans-Euphrates/beyond the River) (d:gungal written with a capital: the land across the Euphrates, mostly Eufrates Gungal gam, the province Trans-Euphrates) (e:Eufrates ~ gam bup tungah aana zang) (b:gungal) (r:15.4.20/6.24.3) (q:draft)
Kenaz = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Kenaz) (e:Zefo, Gatam, leh ~ ahi hi) (r:1.36.11/13.1.53) (q:draft)
Kenaz = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kenizzite) (d:in Kenaz mite, the Kenizzites) (e:Ken mite, ~ mite, Kadmon mite) (r:1.15.19) (q:draft)
Vantung = (t:n) (w:heaven/sky) (d:vantung written with a capital, mostly in Vantung Gam, the kingdom of heaven) (e:~ Gam in ama nasemte ciamtehna lai) (b:vantung) (r:40.18.23/1.1.8) (q:draft)
Kaisar = (t:name) (w:Caesar) (d:title of the Roman emperor, usually Kaisar kumpipa) (e:~ kumpipa kiangah siah piak tuak) (r:42.20.22/42.2.1) (q:draft)
Ahasu = (t:todo) (q:draft, part of the hyphenated word Ahasu-eras meaning Ahasuerus or Xerxes, not a word by itself)
Hor = (t:name) (c:mountain) (w:Hor) (d:in Hor Mual, Mount Hor) (e:Edom gamgi ~ Mual ah Topa in) (r:4.20.23/4.20.25) (q:draft)
Hor = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Horite) (d:in Hor mite, the Horites) (e:amaute mai-ah ~ mite a suksiat) (r:5.2.22) (q:draft)
Gog = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Gog) (e:Tubal minamte a ukpipa ~ aw) (r:26.38.3/13.5.4) (q:draft)
Lianpen = (t:adj) (w:Most High/greatest) (d:lian great with pen most, written with a capital in titles: A Lianpen Pasian, the Most High God, and Siampi Lianpen, the High Priest) (e:A ~ Pasian in kei tungah lim) (b:lianpen) (r:27.4.2/42.1.32) (q:draft)
Ci = (t:n) (w:salt) (d:ci salt written with a capital in place names: Ci Tuipi the Salt Sea or Dead Sea, Ci Kuam the Valley of Salt, Ci Khuapi the City of Salt) (e:gamgi in ~ Tuipi mong) (b:ci) (r:6.15.2/13.18.12) (q:draft)
Dagon = (t:name) (w:Dagon) (d:god of the Philistines) (e:~ biakinn sungah ama lutang suang uh hi) (r:13.10.10/9.5.2) (q:draft)
Jabesh = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Jabesh) (d:town in Gilead, also called Jabesh Gilead) (e:~ khua sunga makeng kung nuai-ah) (r:9.31.13/9.11.9) (q:draft)
Jabesh = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Jabesh) (d:father of Shallum) (e:~’ tapa Shallum in amah sawmsim a) (r:12.15.10) (q:draft)
Ken = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Kenite) (d:in Ken mi and Ken mite, the Kenites) (e:~ mite, Kenaz mite, Kadmon mite) (r:1.15.19/9.30.29) (q:draft)
Ken = (t:n) (w:cliff/precipice) (d:ken written with a capital at the start of a sentence; Ken pang-a means on the side of a cliff) (e:~ pang-a vakhu bu bawl bangin) (r:24.48.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
Anah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Anah) (e:Hiv mi Zibeon’ tapa ~’ tanu Oholibamah) (r:1.36.2/1.36.20) (q:draft)
Er = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Er) (e:Judah’ ta masa ~ pen) (r:1.38.7/1.38.3) (q:draft)
Hanan = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hanan) (e:Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, ~) (r:16.10.10/13.8.23) (q:draft)
Ehud = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ehud) (e:~ a sih khit ciangin Israel mite) (r:7.4.1/7.3.26) (q:draft)
Thukhamna = (t:n) (w:Law/law) (d:the Law of Moses) (e:~ sungah bang a kigelh hiam) (b:Thukham) (r:42.10.26/43.7.51) (q:draft)
Tuiphumpa = (t:n) (w:Baptist/baptizer) (d:the man who baptizes, title of John in Tuiphumpa Johan, John the Baptist) (e:a kici pen ~ Johan ahi hi) (r:40.11.14/40.17.13) (q:draft)
Zif = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ziph) (d:town and desert in Judah; Zif mite means the Ziphites) (e:Saul kiang Gibeah ah ~ mite hong pai) (r:9.26.1/14.11.8) (q:draft)
Harim = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Harim) (e:a thumna ~ tung, a lina Seorim tung) (r:13.24.8/15.2.32) (q:draft)
Paran = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Paran) (d:usually Paran gamlak, the Desert of Paran) (e:~ gamlakah giahphual a sat uh hi) (r:4.12.16/1.21.21) (q:draft)
Pekah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Pekah) (e:Remaliah’ tapa ~ sawl ding kipan hi) (r:12.15.37/12.15.31) (q:draft)
Marka = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Mark) (e:Barnabas in ~ kici Johan sap ding) (r:44.15.37/55.4.11) (q:draft)
Mi = (t:n) (w:person/man/one) (d:mi written with a capital at the start of a quoted line or in a title such as Mi Siangtho, the Holy One) (e:~ tawh kibatna-ah a suak hi) (b:mi) (r:50.2.7/44.3.14) (q:draft)
Siampi = (t:n) (w:Priest/priest) (d:siampi written with a capital as a title before a name or in Siampi Ukpa, the High Priest) (e:a kip tawntung ~ Ukpa a suah) (b:siampi) (r:58.6.20/11.1.26) (q:draft)
Ta = (t:n) (w:Son/son) (d:ta written with a capital, used of Christ as the Son and in titles such as David’ Ta, Son of David) (e:Khazih in David’ ~ hi bangci) (b:ta) (r:42.20.41/43.14.13) (q:draft)
Tausang = (t:n) (w:tower) (d:tower, capitalised as part of the name of a particular tower) (e:Hananel’ ~, tua ciangin Mi Za Khat) (r:16.12.39/7.9.46) (q:draft)
Uzza = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uzzah/Uzza) (e:~ tungah Topa hehin daan pia) (r:13.13.11/15.2.49) (q:draft)
Zeru = (t:todo) (q:draft, part of the hyphenated name Zeru-iah meaning Zeruiah, not a word by itself)
Zin = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zin) (d:desert region in the far south of Canaan, in the phrase Zin gamlak, the Desert of Zin) (e:~ gamlak panin Edom pang teng) (r:4.34.3/6.15.1) (q:draft)
